From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:40:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: the GPU module from pci.hidd and HIDD relations

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: the GPU module said "Not supported on AROS". AROS enumerates
display controllers in pci.hidd and installs pci.ids in DEVS:; since
hiddclass 1.3 (AROS mainline, 2026-11) a display driver declares the PCI
device it runs, and nvgfx's sensors declare the device they measure.
Solution: list the PCI display functions (class 0x03, without auxiliary
functions) as GPUs, named by the upstream pci.ids code reading
DEVS:pci.ids (memmem provided for it). With relations: the driver's name,
VRAM and GART from drivers that measure them (nvgfx; amdgpu and
vmwaresvga answer the framebuffer size), and with the temp option the
current reading of a thermal zone or a "Temperature" telemetry entry
that monitors the device, in its unit. Relation, telemetry and device
path numbers are stated for older SDKs and checked against newer
headers; on an older hiddclass none of those methods is called.
Firmware framebuffers and the software rasterizer name no GPU.
Scope: detection/gpu (gpu_aros.c, gpu_aros_values.c, gpu.h for
FF_GPU_HAS_PCI_IDS), common/aros/aros_memmem, CMakeLists.txt; AROS only.
Upstream-Status: AROS-specific.
Verification: host tests GpuValues and Memmem; guest runs in the port's
records (tests/aros/gpu.script, tests/aros/gpuprobe.c).
Removal: with upstream AROS support.
